{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"785f2fd491d77989c32919266846d8e7bcedc69bbfbcb7f36b90a4c1debea4a9","slug":"uniform","location":"/content/part-1/01-uniform.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"When Nothing Favors Anything","content_includes_title":false,"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"01-uniform.md","url":"/build/01-uniform-69a845df9491b09ce875d03908a1685b.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you’ll learn","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"gacUAboqGy"}],"key":"pQoAHp0TqX"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why some uncertain situations are indifferent rather than complex","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"xqN3J5C6zO"}],"key":"gTEwVs4XAi"}],"key":"XdM2nVcFZQ"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to recognize randomness with no internal structure to exploit","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"NbWBiDBpO7"}],"key":"usl9WJDx0K"}],"key":"Z36QcDuKWC"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why repetition does not always produce learning or advantage","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"xc45hyDpXG"}],"key":"MpYt7NCsvh"}],"key":"Bs0Na7ATyS"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When persistence, strategy, and interpretation stop making sense","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"Db38YhBaBl"}],"key":"G7BqR2OpUt"}],"key":"t666UVxXKY"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to avoid reading meaning, fairness, or progress into indifferent outcomes","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"ff38kRByN0"}],"key":"abmM3LwRky"}],"key":"cEjiiWnk9t"}],"key":"xSw6CC826f"}],"class":"key-idea","key":"Mqd1hdEZz0"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you could imagine a perfectly random situation, what comes to your mind?","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"caoV2ppoek"}],"key":"cKhYEqY80C"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you’re like me, you probably think about some game experiments or tricks, like tossing a coin or throwing a gambling die.","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"lGTVRzzcrs"}],"key":"wnlRFBtoIb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are standard, textbook examples of a particular kind of randomness in which the outcome of some action is completely unpredictable.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"CEmuW8vlp1"}],"key":"almJ9EVxop"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"But, what does it mean exactly to say that the outcome is unpredictable? While the answer seems simple (the face the coin lands on, or the top number shown on the die once it stops turning), it takes a bit more thought to describe this randomness in more detail.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"eZo0ASoE3s"}],"key":"IRfFQQYAau"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Namely, in both of these cases we have a set of ","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"U24QfrdqHm"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"possible outcomes","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"nS60zwFnJS"}],"key":"FTxFffzQJ6"},{"type":"text","value":". In the case of the coin, only two (heads and tails), and in the case of the die, six (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6). These possible outcomes form a set and we’ll call such a set ","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"MSFVMobZoI"},{"type":"span","class":"highlight","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the range","key":"znUNxaOD6q"}],"key":"AK6a6vqWqm"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"GHxXgH3uXQ"}],"key":"GHGeC9xJz3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In probability theory and statistics, the outcome of some random situation is called ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"RcZ2vtvUZD"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"a random variable","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"FrKgtVskmG"}],"key":"rrydGIZTzQ"},{"type":"text","value":" and this set is called the range of the random variable. Every uncertain situation in life will have a range; you can think of it a set of all possibilities that can occur after some action takes place. Philosophers love describing these as ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"Ru6c19Hi07"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"possible worlds","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"AslHIPVwLU"}],"key":"gjfYJyfZPd"},{"type":"text","value":" and if you’re a fan of science fiction, you’ll immediately think of the multiverse. If you do, you’ll not be far off the mark.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"edaEXY1DxV"}],"key":"fgckqdUgs2"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A world that doesn’t care","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"FujIk3dnHQ"}],"identifier":"a-world-that-doesnt-care","label":"A world that doesn’t care","html_id":"a-world-that-doesnt-care","implicit":true,"key":"l0DxhaSBrf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What makes situations like the coin toss and die throw unique is that their unpredictability is not particularly complex. Even a five year old playing a board game can understand how it works. It’s unpredictability, however, stems from the fact that the result that occurs is ","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"scuOzBCG3s"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"completely indifferent","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"sSm64EvmiU"}],"key":"gOn3iLS0bO"},{"type":"text","value":" towards all outcomes in the range; not of them are preferred. When you toss a die, you’re equally likely to get a 1 and a 6. No result is nudged forward, and if the die is fair (not interfered with intentionally), there are no mysterious forces behind it.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"h7cr9hSY3t"}],"key":"SastteTbDM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This particular kind of randomness is called ","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"L8olLkxcXY"},{"type":"span","class":"highlight","children":[{"type":"text","value":"uniform","key":"oIu5X034q1"}],"key":"jAQIDy4IWX"},{"type":"text","value":" randomness, and a set of possible outcomes together with their propensity to occur following a particular pattern is called a ","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"v4yWVUxkvH"},{"type":"span","class":"highlight","children":[{"type":"text","value":"uniform distribution","key":"NneiE99Oci"}],"key":"ezzIrG9HOE"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"VQE8qo3ayT"}],"key":"SFSdcneDlg"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key idea","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"X58stGgivJ"}],"key":"WQs0oy9v5y"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some uncertainty exists because nothing is pushing outcomes anywhere. We call such uncertainty uniform.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"ec9m7mLwpO"}],"key":"Vsecv5vosr"}],"class":"key-idea","key":"mCr3bVW1vR"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why our minds struggle with indifference","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"QENLC8NIGS"}],"identifier":"why-our-minds-struggle-with-indifference","label":"Why our minds struggle with indifference","html_id":"why-our-minds-struggle-with-indifference","implicit":true,"key":"R5DzCB7p1w"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This kind of uncertainty feels oddly clean. There is no sense that effort will help, or that learning more will reveal a pattern. You can wait, retry, hope, or worry, (or try some of the gambling superstitions like blowing the dice) but none of that changes how the situation behaves.","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"yNE1vPpEK3"}],"key":"ukSKiKGkGM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is, perhaps, what makes these situations psychologically uncomfortable for most of us. We are deeply inclined to believe that the world leans somewhere; that outcomes cluster, that persistence pays off, that unfairness hides a reason. But here, the world refuses to cooperate with that instinct. It offers no signal to latch onto.","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"WSRKvoZzXs"}],"key":"v5Kj46Lxyw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The reason could be the fact that humans have evolved to recognize structure.","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"YdkVbBzaVv"}],"key":"WvSmmA0lC9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We are extremely good at noticing patterns, trends, gradients, and deviations. This ability is adaptive in most environments. It helps us learn, improve, and coordinate action. When the world responds to effort or feedback, pattern recognition is a strength.","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"DDMjg1KbW1"}],"key":"POq6oJEJW6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"But, uniform uncertainty offers none of that.","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"rWuist682Z"}],"key":"vk2klEDYkL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Our minds find it very hard to deal with this. When outcomes are scattered evenly, no matter what we do, our mind refuses to interpret this as absence of any structure, but as evidence of some hidden forces beneath. We assume we are missing something. We search harder, watch more closely, and if none of that gives us answers we seek (as it can’t), we reach for conspiratorial explanations.","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"xxh5eyNxIZ"}],"key":"ZY4ehBfn08"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the root of one of the most common errors people make, especially in gambling contexts. Go to Las Vegas, observe the casino tables and you’ll see plenty of examples like this one: roulette wheel lands on black five times in a row. Players will start crowding red, convinced that balance must assert itself. Others will double down on black, believing the streak has momentum. Neither of these interpretations are true.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"AMveTE2vK8"}],"key":"iKyiD4p7pS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can probably feel this pull yourself. Flip a coin 10 times. If you get 9 heads and 1 tail, you’ll start being suspicious that something is wrong with the coin.","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"bq3sHGxEea"}],"key":"Axdnujbwln"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Similarly, you might feel uneasy about number 13. And you’d not be the only one. If you pay attention, you’ll notice that most buildings in the US don’t have the 13th floor.","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"T2EDb93ceH"}],"key":"AmnIovaBV7"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mystical interpretations of uniformly random events do not stop at gambling tables or beliefs about certain numbers. When people experience repeated failure or loss in domains governed by chance (such as death, illness, infertility, etc), they often search for hidden reasons: fate, punishment, destiny, imbalance, moral cause. The mind struggles to accept that something deeply meaningful can be governed by indifference.","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"OjOH2rCo6V"}],"key":"ND0FdQVtiH"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"But it can, and there’s nothing we can do about it.","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"key":"Za3tDVuM0r"}],"key":"BpkMOLM2tI"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pitfall: Beware of conspiratorial thinking","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"Nnuay9I88R"}],"key":"iRdfmDpa9S"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some processes are indifferent to outcomes, and if several random occurences happen, it doesn’t mean there are secret forces behind them. Uniform uncertainty often invites false meaning-making.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"kklKEmDOMK"}],"key":"QJlO5bnua4"}],"class":"pitfall","key":"nH0wjmTZ7z"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Shape of the Situation","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"yfE3DqoUqW"}],"identifier":"the-shape-of-the-situation","label":"The Shape of the Situation","html_id":"the-shape-of-the-situation","implicit":true,"key":"JyBXC8nRvJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The defining feature of this type of uncertainty is that every possibility (every outcome in its range) stands on equal footing.","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"OoiYz7CAqb"}],"key":"O1e3S5MpOY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you imagine this as the space of possible outcomes, it is flat. It has no hills, or valleys. Just an even spread, where every result is as plausible as the next, and none contains information about what should follow.","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"ZZXdyiM7co"}],"key":"TCHYCnTQdM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This does not mean outcomes cannot surprise us. They often do. But the surprise carries no lesson. Nothing about an unexpected result makes the next one more predictable, or more favorable, or more revealing.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"OCL8hgjO92"}],"key":"iYK9AjHnel"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is randomness without internal structure to exploit.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"Shsg1CM3sd"}],"key":"kujQ6daQhX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And that absence of structure is exactly what distinguishes uniform uncertainty from every other shape you will encounter in this book. Later chapters will introduce situations where outcomes cluster, where history matters, where rare events dominate, or where small differences grow into large ones.","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"Lj9lctJuOH"}],"key":"CWhKDTKKg9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here, none of that happens.","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"freyeZOkx5"}],"key":"O90gAG7aGE"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the baseline. The simplest case. The point of zero curvature.","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"kUAGlqUPmC"}],"key":"JrWav63nFY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understanding this shape matters not because it is common (it isn’t) but because it provides contrast. Once you grasp what true indifference looks like, structure becomes visible everywhere else.","position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"key":"ZpSVLBKDQi"}],"key":"MRf8Fqz3vu"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before we can talk about learning, persistence, risk, or strategy, we have to recognize the rare situations where none of those ideas apply.","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"efJCw1GRYk"}],"key":"cTB9xTQtwI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":90,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uniform uncertainty is one of them.","position":{"start":{"line":90,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"key":"UBDP1XhmHr"}],"key":"v4fpr3GNB4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And it is fitting that we talk about this type of uncertainty first, because it is as random as it can possibly get. It offers us nothing to hold on to, there are no creases on its surface we could grab, there are no details on its body to give any sense of distinction. It is pure and unadulterated randomness; chaos in the full sense of the word.","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"MjKLa2tfR5"}],"key":"Sn4m7T2hwR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":94,"column":1},"end":{"line":94,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll use visuals to describe these shapes in more detail, and below you will find the first one of these. What you see here is a chart showing the frequency of a die toss after 1,000 throws.","position":{"start":{"line":94,"column":1},"end":{"line":94,"column":1}},"key":"HwTf4eWfrH"}],"key":"RADDefvb7A"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"When we say that a probability distribution is flat, we mean (visually) something like this: all bars a